{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/812411-the-merciful-in-2e-and-non-murderous-slashers","id":812411,"title":"The Merciful in 2e, and non-murderous Slashers.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-19T23:29:05-08:00","id":812411,"title":"The Merciful in 2e, and non-murderous Slashers.","content":"I know its always hit or miss when comparing World of Darkness compared to Chronicles of Darkness, but... with recycled names and concepts, tye overs, I don't mind mentioning my favorite OWoD hunters--the Merciful. For those unfamiliar with OWoD terms, Hunters came in three flavours. The Zealous want to destroy monsters, or are otherwise antagonists to them. they apply to TS:V, Ashwood Abbey, the Union. The Visionary were Hunters who wanted to understand the supernatural, like.. well, the bulk of Hunter groups. But the Merciful wanted to FIX the supernatural, heal monsters, make them human again. I think this is a faction of Hunter that NEEDS representation in 2e. Null Mysteries might be considered Merciful.. but... I think Hunters filling that role needs to have a place in 2e. A compact helping vampires reach golconda, prometheans reach second dawn, mummies apotheosis... a Compact helping monsters retain their integrity stat. Things like that. Id love to see groups of hunters actively HELPING monsters, even if other hunters distrust them. Its an element that hasnt shown well in Hunter thusfar. But now.. take that to a Slasher extreme. Are there Slashers who dont just hunt and kill humans? Can a Slasher be a Visionary, who disects humans to understand? are there Merciful Slashers, who can't trust humanity to its own devices? Can a Slasher, like a Hunter, exist for more than just the kill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T23:41:05-08:00","id":812413,"title":"","content":"You do know a slasher is, well, a person who slashes at people right? It's in the name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T23:49:25-08:00","id":812414,"title":"","content":"Lucifuge are ironically the Merciful in nWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T01:01:42-08:00","id":812432,"title":"","content":"And the Long Night is a compact from the core book that has at least some interest in fixing monsters \u2014 so much so that C&amp;C's bonus material for them includes guidelines for \u201cSystems of Mercy\u201d, ranging from getting a bonus from being kind to a monster all the way up to reversing the monster's condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T08:48:42-08:00","id":812641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/812411-the-merciful-in-2e-and-non-murderous-slashers?p=812413#post812413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know a slasher is, well, a person who slashes at people right? It's in the name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kills with kindness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:23:32-08:00","id":812670,"title":"","content":"I could see a Slasher who imprisions, rapes, or mutiliates their victims instead of murder, but a friendly slasher that attacks victims with kindness no, it wouldn't be a slasher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:44:30-08:00","id":812685,"title":"","content":"The closest I can think of that may fit that description may be someone like Annie Wilkes from <i>Misery</i>, who is so deluded and lost in her own world that she doesn't necessarily register her actions. She kidnaps her favorite writer, forces him to write a new book to her own liking, and kills anyone who comes near so that the writer isn't discovered. She also hobbles his feet when she realizes that he's almost strong enough to escape on his own. She definitely has her own agenda when it comes to what she wants, but she doesn't necessarily go out just to kill. It's more of an easy way to solve an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T10:39:53-08:00","id":812712,"title":"","content":"As others have said, the Long Night's Merciful are the clearest expression of the Merceful creed in Vigil. There's others though, the Talbot Group for example are pretty much a completely Merciful Compact, and the Lucifuge have elements of mercy too.<br /> <br /> I think that's how I'd like it. I prefer a Hunter with specific beliefs that lead them to be merciful, rather than groups who're defined by being all mercy all the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the Slasher. IMO if they don't murder mortals they're not a Slasher. However a Slasher's primary goal doesn't have to be murder, that can just be a side effect. If you look at Wardens in my homebrew sig for example. They're serial killers, but they could theroterically function happily without killing if they lived in isolation away from any &quot;threats&quot; to overreact too.<br /> <br /> That said, I would say the minimum kills for a Slasher is one, without a kill you don't get the mechanical parts of the template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:20:52-08:00","id":812746,"title":"","content":"A slasher who doesn't kill is like a vampire who doesn't drink blood or a werewolf who can't shapeshift. Killers are what they <i>are. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:25:21-08:00","id":812957,"title":"","content":"I point out though, that with Secrets of the Covanants there is an Invicticus Oath that means you don't drink blood.<br /> <br /> Which is what I'm getting at with Slashers. They're all compelled to kill, but in rare circumstances you can put them in a sitation where their compulsion doesn't trigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:59:59-08:00","id":813018,"title":"","content":"If you're under the assumption that all Hunters in 2e are becoming Slashers, I don't think that's the direction the developers are taking things at all.<br /> <br /> Which means that while Slashers are highly unlikely to fit the Merciful's themes, we could yet see organisations that are more Merciful in nature (and hopefully not religious, one of my big issues with the Long Night is that while I really like their attitude, I just can't stomach their religious bent. Same with the Lucifuge, to a lesser extent).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T05:03:11-08:00","id":813290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/812411-the-merciful-in-2e-and-non-murderous-slashers?p=812746#post812746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A slasher who doesn't kill is like a vampire who doesn't drink blood or a werewolf who can't shapeshift. Killers are what they <i>are. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go further and add that killing is <i>how</i> they are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T06:13:46-08:00","id":813319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/812411-the-merciful-in-2e-and-non-murderous-slashers?p=812746#post812746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A slasher who doesn't kill is like a vampire who doesn't drink blood or a werewolf who can't shapeshift. Killers are what they <i>are. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say rather a werewolf who doesn't <i>hunt.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}